  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-12-01T05:15:25.196Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "You have 2 Options when creating a group, a public & private group. \n\nMy biggest issue with this update is that \"Group\" Instances are by default Group-Members only. \n\nHow-about, whether a VRC Group is public or private determines whether or not people can join \"Group\" Instances. \n\nPublic Group - \"Group\" Instances are joinable for friends+ and members in that group \n\n- This stops the possibility of changing the status of the \"Instance\" which isn't a good feature. There already is orange+, there doesn't need to be a second barrier to cross\n\n*COUGH* Friends that used orange status & are always in invite+/invite instances \n\nPrivate groups since their more exclusive, hence their group instances would be equivalent to traditional private instances without the bench mark of requesting to join the lobby",
